    "summary": "Asafo flag with two headless corpses. The base cloth is of imported green and red silk damask. Base cloth of green and red floral damask, which is edged on three sides with alternating red and white cotton squares, plus a white cotton fringe. There is a wide strip with cotton ties on the fourth side. The central design on both sides shows two soldiers, one in red and one in black holding a red sword; at their feet lie two heads cut from corpses which lie beside them in white. A version of the Union Jack in red and white cotton has been sewn down onto an upper corner.",
